  "mainEntity": {
    "name": "Can Kitchen Lighting Be Upgraded Without Replacing Cabinets?",
    "text": "Can Kitchen Lighting Be Upgraded Without Replacing Cabinets?",
    "@type": "Question",
    "answerCount": 1,
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "text": "Whether kitchen lighting can be upgraded without major remodeling depends on the fixtures, wiring, ceiling access, cabinet design, and desired controls. Replacing a comparable fixture may be relatively limited, while adding recessed lights, under-cabinet wiring, new switches, or circuits can expand the electrical scope and may require permits and inspections.",
